# publish(Handed); const callee = flag ? unknown : other ? Handed : Kept; new callee(); callee()
# A callee that may be anything. The unknown object stands for `Handed`, which has escaped, and with the limit of this test one is many: the construction leaves it out as the call does.
# `Kept` has not escaped: only the list says that it is entered here, so it stays whatever the number.
# The same program with the limit as it is: callee-list-of-a-construction-keeps-the-few-that-have-escaped.ir
# OPTIONS: limit=MaxValueFlowMembersToldApart:0
# RUN: valueflow-apply
# CHECK-LABEL: function f0 name="main"
# CHECK: = Construct v10 {{*}}callees=[f2, ..]
# CHECK: = Call v10 {{*}}callees=[f2, ..]
# PROGRAM-OF: callee-list-of-a-construction-keeps-the-few-that-have-escaped.ir
